Input: {"question": "When was General Bradshaw born?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d00", "start": 0, "end": 141, "text": "Adrian Bradshaw General Sir Adrian John Bradshaw, (born 1958) is a British Army officer who served as Deputy Supreme Allied Commander Europe."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d00", "start": 142, "end": 236, "text": "He also served as Director Special Forces from 2006 to 2009 and Commander Land Forces in 2013."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d00", "start": 237, "end": 398, "text": "He was educated at Bloxham School, the University of Reading (BSc, 1979) and King's College London (MSc Defence Studies, 1991; MA International Relations, 2005)."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d00", "start": 399, "end": 467, "text": "Bradshaw was commissioned into the 14th/20th King's Hussars in 1980."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d00", "start": 468, "end": 574, "text": "In 1994 he became Commanding Officer of the King's Royal Hussars commanding the KRH Battlegroup in Bosnia."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d00", "start": 575, "end": 632, "text": "On promotion to Brigadier he became Senior Advisor to the"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d01", "start": 0, "end": 556, "text": "4 languages العربية Deutsch فارسی Nederlands Edit links Article Talk English Read Edit View history Tools Tools move to sidebar hide Actions Read Edit View history General What links here Related changes Upload file Permanent link Page information Cite this page Get shortened URL Download QR code Print/export Download as PDF Printable version In other projects Wikimedia Commons Wikidata item Appearance move to sidebar hide From Wikipedia , the free encyclopedia British Army general For the British pho