1999) was a senior British Army officer and doctor."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 173, "end": 243, "text": "He served as Director General Army Medical Services from 1977 to 1981."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 244, "end": 279, "text": "Bradshaw was born on 1 August 1920."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 280, "end": 361, "text": "He was educated at Newport High School, a comprehensive school in Newport, Wales."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 362, "end": 441, "text": "He studied medicine at Westminster Hospital Medical School, graduating in 1945."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 442, "end": 552, "text": "Bradshaw was commissioned into the Royal Army Medical Corps, British Army, on 9 November 1946 as a lieutenant."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 553, "end": 599, "text": "He was promoted to captain on 9 November 1947."}, "D5S8": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d04", "start": 600, "end": 620, "text": "On 24 November 1948,"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d05", "start": 0, "end": 51, "text": "which spent the next two years in Northern Ireland."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d05", "start": 52, "end": 232, "text": "Removed from that command due to combat-inexperience in 1944, he succeeded Berney-Ficklin as GOC of the lower establishment 48th Infantry (Reserve) Division (a training formation)."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d05", "start": 233, "end": 266, "text": "He retired from the army in 1946."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0323-29f5e6ffd7be:d05", "start": 267, "end": 413, "text": "Willi